      "hidden_reasoning": "The opponent's Dragapult mirrors mine exactly - same Life Orb set with Draco Meteor, Shadow Ball, Flamethrower, and U-turn, and since it's a copy of my team it likely shares my 213 Speed, outpacing Garchomp's 158. I'm also checking whether their Gholdengo carries a Choice Scarf at 149 base speed.\n\nWorking through the damage math: Dragapult's Draco Meteor would likely one-shot Garchomp given the speed and type disadvantage, so I should expect to lose that Pokémon on switch-in. A scarfed Gholdengo at 223 Speed would outrun my Dragapult though, and since it's Steel/Ghost, Shadow Ball actually hits it super effectively while Draco Meteor is only resisted - so Gholdengo isn't a safe switch against my Dragapult's Shadow Ball.\n\nGarchomp might barely survive Shadow Ball but Draco Meteor would finish it off, and since both are at the same speed tier, staying in is a gamble on which move the opponent picks. Switching to Gholdengo only pays off if Dragapult doesn't lead with Shadow Ball, since Draco would just be resisted anyway — overall it seems like a coin flip either way depending on the opponent's choice.\n\n",
